      "answer": "The Financial Advisory and Intermediary Services (FAIS) Act is credited with raising intermediary professionalism, despite remaining concerns about customer outcomes. [fsca_rdr_2014, p.3, EXECUTIVE SUMMARY]\n\nThe FAIS Act has clearly raised the standards of professionalism and the management of conflicts of interest in the financial advice and intermediary services sector through provisions including a statutory fiduciary duty for intermediaries, transparent disclosure of remuneration arrangements, specific prohibitions and disclosures regarding conflicts of interest, and increased levels of intermediary professionalism through competence, integrity, operational, and compliance requirements. [fsca_rdr_2014, p.11-12, 1.4.1]\n\nHowever, despite this detailed compliance framework, remaining concerns about the potential for mis-selling and poor outcomes for customers have continued to fuel debate as to whether more fundamental structural interventions in the regulatory framework are necessary. [fsca_rdr_2014, p.11-12, 1.4.1]",
      "citation_contract_pass": true,
